<section>
  <div class=3D"wrap">
    <div class=3D"section-head">
      <span class=3D"section-num">04</span>
      <h2>What each layer owns</h2>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"layer-grid">
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag">Config</span>
        <h3>ConfigReader / TestData</h3>
        <p>Reads <code>config.properties</code> once; any key is overridabl=
e with a matching <code>-D</code> system property, so CI can flip browser/h=
eadless/thread-count without touching source.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>base.url</code>, <code>browser</code>, <code>headless</=
code></li>
          <li><code>explicit.wait.seconds</code>, timeouts</li>
          <li>SauceDemo's four fixed user accounts</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag">Driver</span>
        <h3>DriverFactory</h3>
        <p>One creation path per browser; Selenium Manager resolves the dri=
ver binary itself, so nothing browser-version-specific is checked into the =
repo.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>ThreadLocal&lt;WebDriver&gt;</code> =E2=80=94 parallel-=
safe</li>
          <li>Chrome / Firefox / Edge, headless-aware</li>
          <li><code>initDriver()</code> / <code>quitDriver()</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag">Waits</span>
        <h3>WaitUtils</h3>
        <p>Wraps Selenium 4's <code>FluentWait</code> so every page object =
gets the same polling interval and ignored-exception set instead of ad hoc =
<code>Thread.sleep</code>.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Visible / clickable / invisible conditions</li>
          <li>Ignores stale-element during polling</li>
          <li>Implicit wait kept at 0 =E2=80=94 explicit only</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag">Diagnostics</span>
        <h3>TestListener / ScreenshotUtils</h3>
        <p>A TestNG <code>ITestListener</code> hooks failure/pass/skip; on =
failure it grabs the current thread's driver and writes a timestamped PNG.<=
/p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>target/screenshots/&lt;test&gt;_&lt;ts&gt;.png</code></=
li>
          <li>Reads whichever driver <em>this</em> thread owns</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

