<section>
  <div class=3D"wrap">
    <div class=3D"section-head">
      <span class=3D"section-num">06</span>
      <h2>Key decisions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class=3D"decision">Selenium Manager,<br>not WebDriverManage=
r</td>
            <td class=3D"why">Built into Selenium 4.6+; one fewer dependenc=
y, and driver resolution happens automatically at <code>new ChromeDriver()<=
/code> time =E2=80=94 nothing to configure per machine.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class=3D"decision">Driver created<br>per test method</td>
            <td class=3D"why"><code>BaseTest</code> opens a fresh <code>Web=
Driver</code> in <code>@BeforeMethod</code>, not per class. Isolation holds=
 under <code>parallel=3D"methods"</code> too, not just <code>"classes"</cod=
e>.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class=3D"decision">Fluent page objects</td>
            <td class=3D"why">Every navigating action returns the destinati=
on page. A misordered step is a compile error, not a runtime <code>NoSuchEl=
ementException</code> three lines later.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class=3D"decision">Explicit waits only<br>(implicit =3D 0)<=
/td>
            <td class=3D"why">Mixing implicit and explicit waits produces i=
nconsistent, hard-to-debug timeouts. <code>WaitUtils</code> is the single s=
ource of polling behavior.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class=3D"decision">Config via properties<br>+ system-proper=
ty override</td>
            <td class=3D"why">One file for local defaults; <code>-Dbrowser=
=3Dfirefox -Dheadless=3Dtrue</code> on the CI command line needs no code ch=
ange.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

